OpenController Hardware Provenance

The OpenController hardware source is licensed under the CERN Open Hardware
Licence Version 2 - Weakly Reciprocal in LICENSE.

The symbols and footprints in the project libraries were drawn for
OpenController, apart from the antenna footprint described below. The QFN-20
footprint was built from the package drawing in WCH's CH572 datasheet; it is
not copied or derived from KiCad's footprint libraries:

* CH572/lib/OpenController.pretty/CH572D_QFN-20_3x3mm_P0.4mm_EP1.8mm_ThermalVias.kicad_mod

Its 3D model is only a reference to the QFN-20 model installed with KiCad; the
model itself is not distributed here.

The 2.4 GHz antenna footprint is copied unchanged from the OpenDongle
hardware (https://github.com/openkeyboard-org/OpenDongle), where
OpenKeyboard.org independently created the antenna footprint, schematic, and
PCB geometry, informed by the published WCH 2.4 GHz reference antenna and its
functional requirements:

* CH572/lib/OpenController.pretty/ANT-F-2-2.4G-0.8MM-FR4-WCH.kicad_mod
* The corresponding antenna placement, ground edge, and via fence in the
  OpenController CH572 PCB

Reference publication: https://github.com/openwch/schpcb_lib

No WCH CAD, footprint, schematic, or artwork file was copied, imported,
converted, or traced. The reference is retained as factual attribution for the
design inspiration; the independently authored OpenKeyboard.org source files
are licensed under CERN-OHL-W-2.0 with the rest of the hardware design.
